  "findings": [
    "The five Grid methods share an offset of +0.250 dB with a spread of only 0.052 dB, which is a family-level systematic rather than noise.",
    "Only LPE, NTC_PinkPEPS and NTC_PinkPEPS-25 exceed the held-out rms, and only by 1.0 to 1.3 times, so the localisation is suggestive rather than established.",
    "Being a pink variant is not itself the marker: the two Grid pink variants sit at +0.24 with the rest of their family, so whatever is left is specific to the NTC pink combination.",
    "Residual does not track encoder size, decoder size or compression factor, so it is not a capacity effect."
  ],
  "held_out_rms_db": 0.405188,
  "limitations": [
    "Residuals come from a fit with eight free weights against eleven targets; the fit itself can redistribute error between methods.",
    "Grid methods resemble each other, so part of their tightness may reflect that similarity rather than a shared cause.",
    "Three methods at roughly one held-out rms is weak evidence and should direct where to look next, not support a conclusion."
  ],
  "note": "Structure of what the best-fit composition leaves behind. Read against the fit's own held-out rms; residuals inside that band are not evidence.",
